  "worked_solution": "The first three terms of the binomial expansion for $(1+x)^{n}$ are given by\n\n$$\n(1+x)^{n}=1+nx+\\frac{n(n-1)}{2!}{x}^{2}+\u22ef.\n$$\n\nBy substituting $x=\\frac{2b}{7}$ and $n=9$ into the above formula, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(1+\\frac{2b}{7})}^{9} & =1+9\\cdot \\frac{2b}{7}+\\frac{9(9-1)}{2!}\\cdot {(\\frac{2b}{7})}^{2}+\u22ef \\\\  & =1+\\frac{18b}{7}+\\frac{9\\cdot 8}{2}\\cdot \\frac{4{b}^{2}}{49}+\u22ef \\\\  & =1+\\frac{18b}{7}+36\\cdot \\frac{4{b}^{2}}{49}+\u22ef \\\\  & =1+\\frac{18}{7}b+\\frac{144}{49}{b}^{2}+\u22ef.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
